        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.848,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "We call these statistical statements. Simply put, a statistical statement is a claim or summary about some phenomenon, expressed in terms of numerical values, proportions, probabilities, or predictions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.147,
            0.849,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "A statistical question is a question that can be answered by collecting data. For example, “How tall are Grade 7 students in our school?” is a statistical question. We expect that not all Grade 7 students have the same height, but we can collect data, analyse it, and make conclusions about the heights that do occur. The question “Typically, are onions costlier in Yahapur or Wahapur?” is also a statistical question. Prices can vary over time. Therefore, answering this question requires us to look at data, analyse it, and come to conclusions making suitable statistical statements."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.309,
            0.622,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "Which of the following are statistical questions?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.34,
            0.607,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "(a) What is the price of a tennis ball in India?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.365,
            0.632,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "(b) How old are the dogs that live on this street?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.389,
            0.827,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "(c) What fraction of the students in your class like walking up a hill?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.414,
            0.402,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "(d) Do you like reading?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.439,
            0.68,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "(e) Approximately how many bricks are in this wall?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.464,
            0.683,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "(f) Who was the best bowler in the match yesterday?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.489,
            0.69,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "(g) What was the rainfall pattern in Barmer last year?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.514,
            0.847,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "The term statistics refers to the study of collecting, organising, analysing, interpreting, and presenting data. In this chapter, we shall encounter some statistical questions and learn how analysing data and graphs can help answer them."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.617,
            0.508,
            0.64
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.2 Representative Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
